{"line":"result","id":"V72-S3-CHALLENGER","measuredAt":"2026-10-17T03:05:00Z","figure":"The two-day run's nightly refit (run-20261017-0030 against run-20261016-1236, twelve hours apart, 0.50 days of newer rows) reads within noise at four horizons and WORSE beyond noise at one: the hour's direction skill fell 1.66 points; the pinball differences are real at three horizons and under the 1% floor at every one; the refit was not adopted (V7.1 had refused it on the same line). The first clause failed; the second (no adoption within noise under seven days newer) held. The failure is the finding: a fit's direction skill moves between fits by more than the hours' sampling noise allows, on a record where no direction skill is distinguishable from zero.","ci":"hour1 direction skill difference [-2.58, -0.69] points; pinball differences 5m +0.0006 [+0.0003, +0.0009], 1h -0.0003 [-0.0005, -0.0000]","verdict":"failed","commit":"8afbc67","registrationHash":"a1462282d4de"}
{"line":"result","id":"V72-S4-CLOCK","measuredAt":"2026-10-17T03:25:00Z","figure":"On run-20261016-0640 and run-20261016-1236 the 80% range at an hour held from 61% (14:00 UTC, the true spread 1.5 times the forecast's, under 70% in all four halves on both records) to 87-88% (23:00 UTC); no band can fail the line on three weeks, the largest half holding 252 outcomes against the 500 asked. By its letter no band fails; in substance the clock is not learned at the open. To be read on Stage 8's year.","ci":null,"verdict":"not measured","commit":"7df6c06","registrationHash":"1c9dc4134609"}
